WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.000
Every four years with the Olympics,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.149
municipalities compete to host the winter and summer games

00:00:12.149 --> 00:00:16.400
and virtually always plunge their cities, and sometimes even their home countries

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.090
into massive debt and insolvency.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.800
Why? Because host cities inevitably spend double or more over initial estimates.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.000
Fewer people show up than expected.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.800
And the International, Olympic Committee, or I.O.C.,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.000
takes bigger and bigger cuts of TV and other revenue streams.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.340
Sports economist Andrews Zimbalist says that a typical summer Olympics

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.000
Generates up to six billion dollars in revenue,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.930
at least half of which goes to the I.O.C.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:46.400
Winter games generate even less money despite often being more expensive to host than summer games.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.980
cities routinely claim that whatever money they spend on new facilities

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.200
will stimulate the local economy for decades to come.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:57.000
With the recent announcement that Paris will host the 2024 summer games

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.800
and Los Angeles will host the 2028 summer games,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.270
Here are five cities that got F*CKED by Hosting the Olympics.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:15.000
Athens is the birthplace of the ancient games that inspired today's modern municipal money pits.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.059
Its 2004 games cost $16 billion or ten times the original estimate.

00:01:21.059 --> 00:01:24.200
By 2010 more than half the venues built for the event

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.700
were underused, completely empty,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.500
or literally falling apart.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.060
At $50 billion the Sochi winter games cost more

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.500
than all previous winter Olympics combined,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.400
paid for by a dwindling supply of Russian petrol dollars and gold bullion.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.000
Boris Nemtsov documented that $21 billion went for embezzlement

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.800
and kickbacks for businessman friends of Vladimir Putin.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.400
Nemtsov was later assassinated.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.780
Plagued by low ticket sales

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.200
and partly due to the outbreak of the zika virus,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.000
the Rio games ended up costing $20 billion

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.400
rather than the $13 billion backers claimed.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.920
And the showplace Maracana Stadium, which got a $500 million makeover,

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.500
Was largely abandoned soon after the games

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.900
and has had thousands of seats ripped out by vandals.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.000
The Beijing games cost $42 billion, a record at the time,

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.610
even though Amnesty International charged that the Chinese government

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.700
used forced labor to build many of the venues.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.000
The I.O.C. didn't mind the stratospheric cost

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.000
or the crackdowns on dissent, though.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.000
It awarded Beijing the 2022 winter games.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:56.200
The mayor of Montreal declared that the Olympics can no more have a deficit than a man can have a baby.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:59.000
Unfortunately it took Montreal 30 years to pay off its debt

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:03.300
just for the main stadium built for the 1976 games.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.589
If there's good news here

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.000
it's that cities seem to be wising up.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.900
Paris and Los Angeles were the only two cities to bid on the 2024 Olympics

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.700
and the I.O.C. was so anxious that there wouldn't be enough applications for 2028

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.200
that it preemptively awarded them to L.A.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.700
But just like with professional sports teams that extort tax dollars and subsidies

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.500
for stadiums that never pay back their inflated costs,

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.900
it's likely the Olympics will keep finding new suckers

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.400
for one of the oldest scams in sports.

